WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:06.310
Hey Youtubers it's Charlie and this weekend
is the season 4 finale so I wanted to rank

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:08.109
the previous finales from season 1 to 3.

00:00:08.109 --> 00:00:11.670
I always like to look back at all of the seasons
after they've come and gone just to see if

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:16.380
I've changed my mind about what my favorite
moments were or things I thought they could

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:17.380
have done better.

00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:21.250
We can totally do that for Season 4 starting
next week, but for now, let's just focus on

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:23.600
that final episode.

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:26.210
If you're finding me for the first time I
do game of thrones videos every week including

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:27.210
episode reviews bonus videos and Q&amp;As.

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:31.230
Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:35.180
I'm even doing a special giveaway this sunday
when I post my finale review.

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:36.200
So this is how we're going to do this.

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:39.890
I'm going to rank each of the previous finales
and re-examine them in the larger context

00:00:39.890 --> 00:00:42.870
of the books and how the show is changing
things.

00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:47.960
Careful for spoilers if you're new to the
show or you haven't watched any episodes.

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:52.160
Here we go Number 3 - The Season 3 Finale

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:55.899
There was so much that happened in this episode
but I feel like everyone still remembers it

00:00:55.899 --> 00:00:58.150
as Red Wedding aftermath.

00:00:58.150 --> 00:01:03.280
It's like the finale episodes each season
are victims of 9th episode oh shit moments.

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:08.570
Everyone is left clinging to this fear-high
from red wedding fumes that Jon and Ygritte

00:01:08.570 --> 00:01:10.630
in the north and even Daenerys in the east
were letdowns.

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:14.970
At no point did I ever feel like any moments
in the season 3 finale were wasted, it's just

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:19.590
that the red wedding was such a cultural landmark
for television, there was no way they were

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:22.960
going to top that until we got to season 4.

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:30.930
I think Yara and Balon Greyjoy opening that
box with Theon's favorite toy and Robb Stark's

00:01:30.930 --> 00:01:35.740
Body with Grey Wind's head on it were the
few things most people remember just because

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:36.880
they were so graphic.

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:45.270
That's really why I made this my number 3,
just because I think they should have made

00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:47.549
the Red Wedding the finale.

00:01:47.549 --> 00:01:52.310
There were so many other important foreshadowing
moments, like Bran passing North of the wall,

00:01:52.310 --> 00:01:55.820
Sam and Maester Aemon sending the raven to
Stannis about the white walkers.

00:01:55.820 --> 00:02:01.979
I think my favorite moment from the finale
wasn't Daenerys or Theon's surprise box, it

00:02:01.979 --> 00:02:04.860
was Ser Davos helping Gendry escape.

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:08.729
Not just because Gendry is a fan favorite
and everyone wants him to find Arya again,

00:02:08.729 --> 00:02:13.280
but because I believe there is a divine plan
for everyone.

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:17.040
And people survive for a reason.

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:23.040
Gendry rowing aways isn't just a random act
of kindness.

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:28.970
It's like the universe of A Song of Ice and
Fire saying, you are too important to die,

00:02:28.970 --> 00:02:30.980
you are part of a bigger plan.

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:35.510
Yes Dan and Dave have changed George RR Martin's
"plan" a little, but largely I think both

00:02:35.510 --> 00:02:37.599
the books and the show will end at the same
point.

00:02:37.599 --> 00:02:39.769
They'll just get there in slightly different
ways.

00:02:39.769 --> 00:02:42.629
And after Gendry rowed away from Dragonstone
I couldn't stop thinking about what the show

00:02:42.629 --> 00:02:45.489
was going to do with him.

00:02:45.489 --> 00:02:49.760
And we're still wondering.

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:53.480
They could fold the mummer's dragon story
into his, he could head east and join the

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:56.430
golden company or he could run into Arya somewhere
else.

00:02:56.430 --> 00:03:00.459
I can't stop thinking about it and supposedly
Joe Dempsie tweeted that he got to work with

00:03:00.459 --> 00:03:02.280
Maisie Williams this year.

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:07.260
Because his character has changed so much
from the book I have no idea what he's going

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:08.260
to be doing.

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:09.260
So keep your eyes peeled for a cameo in the
finale.

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:12.459
Otherwise we'll have to wait to season 5 to
find out what happened to him.

00:03:12.459 --> 00:03:15.819
On to my second favorite finale - Season 2

00:03:15.819 --> 00:03:20.000
Yes this followed Blackwater, but I don't
feel like the contrast between episodes was

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:22.190
a great as it was in season 3.

00:03:22.190 --> 00:03:25.270
So it was a lot easier for the big holy crap
moments to stand out.

00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:29.720
Like Arya getting the braavosi coin, the army
of white walkers, Theon at Winterfell and

00:03:29.720 --> 00:03:31.460
Daenerys in the house of the Undying.

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:37.061
I feel like the house of the undying was definitely
the most important part even if the white

00:03:37.061 --> 00:03:39.290
walkes were the biggest WTF.

00:03:39.290 --> 00:03:43.659
The house of the undying scenes are part of
the biggest group of prophecies on the show.

00:03:43.659 --> 00:03:47.269
I did a video on my favorite ones, but there
are over 50 big ones in the series.

00:03:47.269 --> 00:03:51.710
The House of the Undying comprises the largest
single concentration of them, so far that

00:03:51.710 --> 00:03:52.710
is.

00:03:52.710 --> 00:03:55.191
I fully expect George RR Martin to eventually
pay off all of the Undying prophecies over

00:03:55.191 --> 00:03:57.140
the course of the rest of the books and I
know the show will do it.

00:03:57.140 --> 00:04:00.930
In a book there aren't any limitations when
it comes to the scope of your story.

00:04:00.930 --> 00:04:04.299
But on a television show it's apocryphal to
tease something major like Daenerys in King's

00:04:04.299 --> 00:04:05.299
Landing in the middle of Winter.

00:04:05.299 --> 00:04:06.299
And then not deliver on it at some point.

00:04:06.299 --> 00:04:09.640
Just for reference, here are some of the biggest
prophecies that came out of the house of the

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:10.690
undying:

00:04:10.690 --> 00:04:19.109
The Dragon Has Three Heads, Mother of Dragons,
Three Fires You Must Light and Daughter of

00:04:19.109 --> 00:04:20.109
Death.

00:04:20.109 --> 00:04:23.050
I'll add a link in the description.

00:04:23.050 --> 00:04:26.240
I explain some of these in greater detail
in that other bonus video.

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:28.900
But on to my number 1 Season Finale.

00:04:28.900 --> 00:04:29.900
- Season 1

00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:32.639
I know it seems weird the way I ranked all
these, like they're getting worse as we go

00:04:32.639 --> 00:04:33.639
along.

00:04:33.639 --> 00:04:34.639
That's not true.

00:04:34.639 --> 00:04:37.000
It's just that in the greater context of the
series and the books.

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:41.880
The season 1 finale had a much greater impact
than the season 2 and 3 finales.

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:46.230
I'm really hoping the season 4 finale changes
the trend.

00:04:46.230 --> 00:04:51.509
Season 1 episode 10 was really the moment
dragons came back into the world.

00:04:51.509 --> 00:04:55.630
It was like Daenerys was proving that magic
does exist.

00:04:55.630 --> 00:04:58.759
Up to that point on the show there wasn't
a lot of proof that there was anything different

00:04:58.759 --> 00:05:02.300
about the show than any other period story.

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:06.610
Westeros without magic and dragons could totally
be medieval western europe.

00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:07.610
The dragons changed that.

00:05:07.610 --> 00:05:11.220
Because once you say dragons exist, it opens
the door for shadow babies, White Walkers

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:12.910
and the stranger knows what else.

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:18.070
To be fair though, the season 1 and two finales
in my mind were equally amazing, but I chose

00:05:18.070 --> 00:05:20.530
season 1 as my favorite just because of daenerys.

00:05:20.530 --> 00:05:24.720
I think that's the scene that made her character
so popular for fans of the show.

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:29.240
HBO started using her face more and more to
market it even though Tyrion in my mind is

00:05:29.240 --> 00:05:30.930
a more important character.

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:39.800
That could always change in one of the future
seasons or books, but Daenerys naked with

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:43.169
dragons is what you think of when you think
of the show.

00:05:43.169 --> 00:05:47.870
If you ever wanted to convince your friends
to watch, that's the gif you'd send them.

00:05:47.870 --> 00:05:49.570
Daenerys naked with baby dragons.

00:05:49.570 --> 00:05:51.280
But now it's your turn.

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:55.940
Which finale has been your favorite so far
and what do you want to see in the season

00:05:55.940 --> 00:05:57.570
4 finale?

00:05:57.570 --> 00:06:01.550
Please use spoiler tags when commenting if
you've read the books.

00:06:01.550 --> 00:06:06.440
Kit Harington was saying there would definitely
be a surprise at the end, he didn't say what,

00:06:06.440 --> 00:06:10.250
but make sure you don't leave your television
till the episode cuts to black.

00:06:10.250 --> 00:06:14.910
I'm just hoping that the Ice and Fire theme
of the finale continues and they end on an

00:06:14.910 --> 00:06:15.910
oh shit moment in the north.

00:06:15.910 --> 00:06:18.900
That could either be something Jon Snow related
or Bran related.

00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:23.960
I'm not expected a white walker scene since
we got that amazing one in episode 4.

00:06:23.960 --> 00:06:25.120
But it's another possibility.

